   "explanation": "Not checked pass/fail. For pay dates before July 1, 2026, PDOC still applies the Prince Edward Island fifth-bracket threshold and constant as first published in the 122nd edition. Probing PDOC on 2026-11-27 (monthly pay dated 2026-03-13 at $11,980 / $12,010 / $12,100 / $13,000 / $17,000 / $20,000) fits A = $142,250 and KP = $6,460 exactly. CRA's current Table 8.1 CSV for 2026 (marked *Updated May 2026) and the 123rd and 124th editions all give $142,520 and KP $6,464 (the 2025 threshold $140,000 indexed by 1.8%). KiddieTrac's table keeps the published, corrected figure; the effect is at most $0.34 a month on PE income over $142,250 for pays dated January-June 2026, which are all in the past. Below that income PDOC and KiddieTrac agree (case PE-H2)."
